{"text": "The software development lifecycle (SDLC) management process begins with the requirement gathering phase, where business analysts and stakeholders collaborate to identify and document the software requirements. Once the requirements are clearly defined, the design phase is initiated, involving system architects and developers who create a blueprint for the software architecture. Meanwhile, project managers develop a project plan that outlines timelines, resources, and milestones. Following the design phase, the development phase commences, where developers write and compile code according to the specifications. At the same time, quality assurance teams prepare test cases and testing environments. Once the development is complete, the testing phase begins, where the software is rigorously tested for bugs and performance issues. If any issues are identified, the development team addresses them, and the software is retested. After successful testing, the deployment phase is initiated, where the software is released to the production environment. During deployment, IT support teams ensure that the software is integrated smoothly with existing systems. Finally, the maintenance phase involves monitoring the software for any issues and implementing updates or patches as necessary to ensure optimal performance and security.", "name": "Software Development Lifecycle Management", "id": 0, "category": "", "tokens": [{"text": "The", "indexInDocument": 0, "posTag": "DT", "sentenceIndex": 0}, {"text": "software", "indexInDocument": 1, "posTag": "NN", "sentenceIndex": 0}, {"text": "development", "indexInDocument": 2, "posTag": "NN", "sentenceIndex": 0}, {"text": "lifecycle", "indexInDocument": 3, "posTag": "NN", "sentenceIndex": 0}, {"text": "(", "indexInDocument": 4, "posTag": "(", "sentenceIndex": 0}, {"text": "SDLC", "indexInDocument": 5, "posTag": "NNP", "sentenceIndex": 0}, {"text": ")", "indexInDocument": 6, "posTag": ")", "sentenceIndex": 0}, {"text": "management"